You are worker AB1 in the OPUS-CAPACITY-CAMPAIGN-20260908 EMC research campaign. This is a bounded, concrete manuscript-writing artifact authorized by the scientific coordinator within an ongoing integration. It is not a new paper, a new approval request, or a new science cycle.

FIRST: read in full `/home/user/Rare-cancers/research/autonomy/opus-capacity-campaign-20260908/COMMON-BRIEF.md`, `CORPUS-CONTEXT.md` and `CLOSED-WORK.md`.

WRITE ISOLATION: you are READ-ONLY with respect to `/home/user/Rare-cancers`. Write nothing there, run no git write operation, edit no manuscript, artifact, graph file, view or report. All your work goes under `/tmp/claude-0/ab1-lane/`. DO NOT delete that directory — the parent will collect it. Record `date -u`, `git rev-parse HEAD` and `git status --porcelain` at start AND end; HEAD moves under you as the parent commits, so verify nothing you measured changed rather than assuming it.

MODEL: report your model as SELF-REPORT, NOT INDEPENDENTLY VERIFIED, and paste the literal output of `env | grep -i -E 'claude|anthropic|model' | sed -E 's/(TOKEN|KEY|SECRET)[^=]*=.*/\1=<redacted>/I'`.

TASK. The accepted working manuscript is `research/manuscripts/dependency/emc-atr-collaborator-package.md` (integrated at commit 1891cd31, title "Reading-frame constraints and retained RG content in NR4A3 fusion models of extraskeletal myxoid chondrosarcoma"). Its abstract currently measures 341 words against a recorded 250-word limit for Genes, Chromosomes and Cancer. Prepare ONE shortened abstract, ISOLATED in your own lane, of AT MOST 250 words by the actual declared counter — aim a little below 250 so there is no edge ambiguity.

The shortened abstract MUST preserve:
- the central contributions of the paper (read the whole manuscript to identify them; do not guess from the abstract alone);
- the honest source and computational limitations;
- that recruitment was NOT measured at intermediate positions on the retained-RG axis;
- the distinction between a REPORTED breakpoint and a MEASURED construct;
- the evaluated-grid qualification on the symmetric prefix sweep (every N-terminal prefix from 50 aa to full length in 10-aa steps; no TCF12 prefix ON THE EVALUATED GRID reaches the lowest value any FET prefix takes on that grid).

MEASURING THE WORD COUNT — this matters. The declared counter is in `research/manuscripts/submission_metrics.py`. That script REWRITES `research/manuscripts/submission-metrics.json` when run, and it does NOT implement `--help`: invoking it with `--help` still executes and writes. DO NOT RUN IT AS A SCRIPT. Instead read its source, identify the exact function it uses to count abstract words, confirm BY READING THE SOURCE that that function writes nothing, and then call that function directly on your candidate text from a `python3 -c` one-liner that imports the module without executing `main()`. Record the exact invocation and its literal output. If you cannot find a write-free path, say so and report the count from a method you describe exactly, labelled as NOT the declared counter.

DELIVERABLES, written into `/tmp/claude-0/ab1-lane/` and left there:
- `BEFORE-abstract.txt` — the current abstract, verbatim, as extracted;
- `AFTER-abstract.txt` — your shortened abstract;
- `abstract.diff` — a unified diff between them;
- `COUNTER-INVOCATION.txt` — the exact command(s) you ran to count and their literal output, with exit codes;
- `NOTES.md` — which sentences you cut, and for each of the five required preservations above, the sentence in your version that carries it.

PROHIBITIONS. Change no preregistered row and no source data. Run no producer, no figure generator, no gate, and no `scripts/preflight.sh`. Do not regenerate any view. Invent no fact, source, number or measurement — every quantity in your abstract must already appear in the manuscript with the same value. Do not add a claim the manuscript does not make. Make no EMC efficacy, safety, selectivity or clinical-readiness claim; there is no wet lab. No network retrieval, no paid API, no GPU, no publication. Do not read, audit, extend or reference `reports/W25-*` or any W25 continuation. If any request of yours is refused by content policy, STOP that branch, record the refusal verbatim, and never route around it.

Stop condition: one abstract at or under 250 words by the declared counter with all five preservations carried, or ~40 tool calls, whichever comes first. Returning early is a success; padding is not.

Your report goes in your final message text. Headings: Worker / Task / Method and inputs / The shortened abstract, in full / Word count with exact counter invocation and output / The five required preservations, each mapped to a sentence / What was cut and why / Limitations / Stop condition / Tool-call count actually used.
